        "original_id": "5e2ebafb-3356-5ec6-b62f-d6798e563bd1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Mount Baker station, Seattle–Tacoma International Airport, Seattle, SeaTac, Downtown Seattle, University of Washington\n- Systems: Link Light Rail system, Central Link line\n- Topics: station location, airport identifiers, regional service\n\nFacts:\n- Mount Baker station is a light rail station in Seattle, Washington.\n- Mount Baker station is between Columbia City station and Beacon Hill station on the Central Link line.\n- The Central Link line is part of the Link Light Rail system and runs from Seattle–Tacoma International Airport to Downtown Seattle and the University of Washington.\n- Seattle–Tacoma International Airport is the primary commercial airport serving the Seattle metropolitan area in Washington.\n- Seattle–Tacoma International Airport is also called Sea–Tac Airport or Sea–Tac.\n- Seattle–Tacoma International Airport has the identifiers IATA SEA, ICAO KSEA, and FAA LID SEA.\n- Seattle–Tacoma International Airport is in the city of SeaTac, about 13 miles south of Downtown Seattle.",
